  <h2>No investment advice</h2>
  <p>
    Everything on this website is for information and education only. It describes my own
    trading strategies and how they have performed. It is not investment advice, not an offer,
    and not a recommendation or solicitation to buy, sell or hold any crypto asset, security,
    derivative or other financial instrument.
  </p>
  <p>
    I am not a licensed financial adviser, investment firm or asset manager, and I do not
    manage money for others. Nothing here takes your personal circumstances, goals or risk
    tolerance into account. Before making any investment decision, do your own research and,
    if needed, consult a qualified, independent adviser.
  </p>

  <h2>My own positions</h2>
  <p>
    I trade the strategies described on this website with my own money. I may therefore hold
    long or short positions in the assets mentioned, and those positions may change at any time
    without notice.
  </p>

  <h2>Risk of loss</h2>
  <p>
    Trading crypto assets is highly risky. Prices can move sharply within minutes, markets can
    become illiquid, and exchanges or tokens can fail. You can lose some or all of the money you
    invest.
  </p>
  <p>
    Some strategies use leveraged products such as perpetual futures. Leverage multiplies gains
    and losses; positions can be liquidated quickly, and losses can exceed the margin you put up.
    Leveraged products are not suitable for everyone.
  </p>

  <h2>Backtests and past performance</h2>
  <p>
    Backtests are simulations of how a strategy would have traded on historical data. They are
    hypothetical: they do not involve real money, and they cannot fully account for fees,
    slippage, funding costs, liquidity, outages or the effect of hindsight when designing a
    strategy. Real trading results usually differ from backtests.
  </p>
  <p>
    Past performance, whether backtested or live, is not a reliable indicator of future results.
    A strategy that has worked in the past can stop working.
  </p>

  <h2>Accuracy</h2>
  <p>
    I prepare the content of this website with care, but I cannot guarantee that it is
    accurate, complete or up to date. Figures may contain errors or be revised later. I accept no
    liability for losses arising from the use of this information, to the extent permitted by
    law.
  </p>
